@* Six real inputs, not one hidden field with painted boxes. The field posts without
   JavaScript, autocomplete="one-time-code" lets the phone offer the code it just received, and
   nothing needs re-hydrating after a fragment swap.

   ui.js adds only what typing expects: advance on entry, retreat AND clear on backspace, and a
   paste of the whole code filling every box. The server sees one value, not six. *@
<InputOtp Name="code" Length="6">
    <InputOtpGroup>
        <InputOtpSlot First AriaLabel="Digit 1 of 6" />
        <InputOtpSlot AriaLabel="Digit 2 of 6" />
        <InputOtpSlot AriaLabel="Digit 3 of 6" />
    </InputOtpGroup>
    <InputOtpSeparator />
    <InputOtpGroup>
        <InputOtpSlot AriaLabel="Digit 4 of 6" />
        <InputOtpSlot AriaLabel="Digit 5 of 6" />
        <InputOtpSlot AriaLabel="Digit 6 of 6" />
    </InputOtpGroup>
</InputOtp>
